// pfodWeb NOTE: dedicated-hardware pin-exclusion audit, 2026-07-12.
// Board: SparkFun Thing Plus - RP2350 (RP2350A + Raspberry Pi RM2 Radio
// Module [CYW43439-based WiFi/BLE SiP], onboard microSD slot, onboard
// 8MB PSRAM). No board.json override existed before this audit - this
// board's pins_arduino.h `#include "../generic/common.h"` for its D<n>/
// A<n>/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/SDA/SCL alias declarations, so without a per-
// board override every GPIO with a common.h alias defaults to full
// digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output via build_boards.js's
// buildEsp32Board() - including GPIO8 (onboard PSRAM chip-select) and
// GPIO9 (onboard microSD chip-select), neither of which is safe or even
// meaningful for a sketch to twiddle as plain digital I/O.
//
// Sources consulted:
//  - This board's own pins_arduino.h (variants/rp2040/rp2040w/
//    sparkfun_thingplusrp2350/pins_arduino.h): `#define PIN_SPI0_SS
//    (9u) // CS pin for SD card`, `#define RP2350_PSRAM_CS (8u)`,
//    `#define PIN_NEOPIXEL (14)` / `NUM_NEOPIXEL (1)`. Authoritative -
//    this is the actual arduino-pico board-support source the generated
//    sketches compile against.
//  - variants/rp2040/rp2040w/generic/common.h - confirms D0-D22/A0-A2/
//    SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/SDA/SCL alias declarations this board inherits,
//    and its own comment block explaining GPIO23/24/25/29 are
//    deliberately NOT declared (assumed CYW43-radio-reserved on Pico-
//    derived boards using this shared fallback - see below).
//  - https://docs.sparkfun.com/SparkFun_Thing_Plus_RP2350/hardware_overview/
//    Official SparkFun hookup guide. Confirms: "The WS2812 Data In pin
//    connects to I/O 14 but we've defined this pin as NEOPIXEL"; "The
//    Qwiic connector is tied to GPIO6 (SDA) and GPIO7 (SCL)"; "The
//    RT9080's EN (Enable) pin is tied to GPIO13" (peripheral power
//    switch, left general-purpose - not dedicated silicon-safety
//    hardware); microSD "connects to the RP2350's SPI bus" (singular);
//    the board's PTH headers "break out a selection of 21 GPIO pins...
//    connections to UART, I2C, SPI, 13 GPIO (3 analog-capable) and the
//    WS2812's DATA OUT pin" - SPI (SCK/MOSI/MISO) is explicitly called
//    out as a header-exposed function group distinct from the plain-
//    GPIO count, confirming SPI0 (GPIO2/3/4) is genuinely dual-purpose
//    (external header SPI break-out, shared internally with the microSD
//    socket) rather than SD-card-exclusive - left general-purpose,
//    matching this repo's existing policy for shared-but-broken-out SPI
//    buses (see sibling vendor board esp32/esp32c6/
//    sparkfun_esp32c6_thing_plus, which likewise leaves its microSD
//    SPI pins IO18-21 at chip-level defaults). GPIO9 (SD chip-select)
//    is NOT among the header pin labels found (SPI-bus lines are header-
//    exposed, the SD card's own dedicated CS is not) - excluded.
//  - Official schematic PDF (docs.sparkfun.com/SparkFun_Thing_Plus_RP2350/
//    assets/board_files/SparkFun_Thing_Plus_RP2350.pdf, rev v1.0):
//    confirms GPIO8 wired as PSRAM chip-select net (APS6404L-3SQR-ZR,
//    8MB QSPI PSRAM, "8MB PSRAM" block - CE pin, separate from the
//    RP2350's dedicated silicon QSPI_SD0-3/QSPI_SCLK/QSPI_CS pads which
//    are shared with the onboard 16MB boot flash and are not part of the
//    GPIO0-29 address space at all); confirms the µSD Card Socket block
//    with its own "**WARNING** Do not set SPI pins high while the µSD
//    card is unpowered, doing so could damage the GPIO pins!" caution
//    note; confirms the radio is the official "Raspberry Pi RM2 Radio
//    Module" (a packaged CYW43439 SiP, not a raw CYW43439-on-board
//    design) - RM2 is Raspberry Pi's own drop-in module specifically
//    designed to replicate the validated Pico 2 W reference wiring
//    (GPIO23/24/25/29), so common.h's existing GPIO23/24/25/29 omission
//    is treated as correct for this board too (this board's own
//    rp2040w/board.json chip-bucket comment already documents this as
//    the intended fix for sparkfun_thingplusrp2350 specifically) - no
//    per-board GPIO23/24/25/29 override added here; the schematic's own
//    net-label text for the RM2<->RP2350 SPI-like control lines was not
//    legibly extractable from the PDF's text layer to independently
//    re-derive the exact GPIO numbers, so this relies on the existing
//    common.h precedent + RM2-replicates-Pico-2W-wiring reasoning rather
//    than a direct schematic net-label read.
//  - Buttons block (same schematic): confirms only BOOT and RESET
//    push-buttons exist. RESET ties to the RP2350's RUN pin (hardware
//    reset, not a GPIO). BOOT is the standard RP2040/RP2350 BOOTSEL-
//    style button (read via the boot ROM, not a normal digitalRead()-
//    capable GPIO on this family) - no "button" capability tag applies,
//    matching this repo's existing convention of never tagging Pico-
//    family BOOTSEL buttons as a general-purpose "button" pin.
//  - LEDs block (same schematic): confirms three fixed-function
//    indicator LEDs (PWR, CHG, STAT) hardwired to power/charge-status
//    circuitry, not user-controllable GPIOs - no additional led_high/
//    led_low tag applies to any GPIO for these. The only user-
//    controllable LED is the WS2812 NeoPixel on GPIO14, already
//    documented above.
//
// GPIO8 (RP2350_PSRAM_CS): CONFIRMED onboard PSRAM chip-select,
// vendor-documented ("8MB PSRAM" block, APS6404L-3SQR-ZR) and confirmed
// directly in this board's own pins_arduino.h. Not broken out to either
// header. No legitimate general-purpose or bus-role capability applies
// (PSRAM CS is never meant to be user-toggled) - capabilities left
// empty, note-only, matching this repo's existing "no legitimate
// hardware alias worth surfacing" precedent (adafruit_trinkeyrp2040qt,
// wiznet_6300_evb_pico).
//
// GPIO9 (PIN_SPI0_SS): CONFIRMED onboard microSD card chip-select
// ("// CS pin for SD card" in this board's own pins_arduino.h; not
// listed among the hookup guide's header-exposed pins). capabilities
// left empty here - build_boards.js's unconditional SS-alias match
// still attaches the correct "spi_ss" bus-role tag on top (that
// vocabulary isn't part of chipGpios' CAP_ORDER, so it can't be
// suppressed and shouldn't be - it correctly reflects the pin's real
// SPI role), but no digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output is offered.
//
// GPIO14 (PIN_NEOPIXEL): CONFIRMED onboard WS2812 addressable RGB LED
// data line, vendor-documented ("WS2812 Data In pin connects to I/O 14
// ... defined this pin as NEOPIXEL") and confirmed in pins_arduino.h
// (NUM_NEOPIXEL=1). Also broken out to the header as "LED_OUT" for
// downstream chaining, per the schematic's Thing Plus Pinout block.
// Tagged capabilities: ["digital_output","led_neopixel","pwm_output"],
// matching this repo's existing led_neopixel precedent (e.g. esp32c61
// GPIO8, sparkfun_esp32c6_thing_plus GPIO23). digital_input dropped -
// the pin is committed to driving the LED, not general-purpose input.
//
// GPIO2/3/4 (PIN_SPI0_SCK/MOSI/MISO): shared between the onboard
// microSD socket and the header-exposed general SPI bus (see sources
// above) - left at chip-derived defaults (no chipGpios override), same
// policy as sibling vendor board sparkfun_esp32c6_thing_plus's microSD
// SPI pins. build_boards.js's unconditional SCK/MOSI/MISO-alias match
// still attaches the correct spi_sck/spi_mosi/spi_miso bus-role tags.
//
// GPIO6/7 (Wire0 SDA/SCL): confirmed Qwiic I2C connector pins - already
// correctly tagged via automatic SDA/SCL alias matching, no override
// needed.
//
// Known pre-existing gap in the shared generic/common.h this board
// relies on (out of scope for this per-board audit - common.h is shared
// by sparkfun_thingplusrp2350/sparkfun_xrp_controller/
// sparkfun_xrp_controller_beta and editing it would affect all three):
// common.h declares D0-D22/A0-A2/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/SDA/SCL aliases but
// no TX/RX aliases, so build_boards.js's g===tx/g===rx serial-role
// detection never fires for this board - GPIO0/GPIO1 surface as plain
// general-purpose D0/D1 pins instead of serial_tx/serial_rx despite
// pins_arduino.h defining PIN_SERIAL1_TX=0/PIN_SERIAL1_RX=1. Flagged in
// boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040w/sparkfun_thingplusrp2350/notes.txt for a
// future dedicated fix; not touched here per task scope (SD/PSRAM/WiFi/
// LED/button pin-capability audit only).
//
// See boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040w/sparkfun_thingplusrp2350/notes.txt
// for the full research trail.
{
  "boardName": "RP2040W",
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico W / 2W",
  "family": "rp2040",
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],
  "connections": ["serial", "tcp", "http", "ble"],
  "pinNotes": {},
  "chipGpios": {
    "8":  { "capabilities": [], "note": "Onboard 8MB PSRAM (APS6404L) chip-select - dedicated, not broken out, not general purpose (confirmed pins_arduino.h RP2350_PSRAM_CS + official schematic)" },
    "9":  { "capabilities": [], "note": "Onboard microSD card chip-select (SPI0 SS) - dedicated, not broken out to header, not general purpose (confirmed pins_arduino.h \"CS pin for SD card\" + official schematic uSD Card Socket block)" },
    "14": { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "led_neopixel", "pwm_output"], "note": "Onboard WS2812 NeoPixel data line (also broken out as header pin LED_OUT for daisy-chaining) - confirmed docs.sparkfun.com hardware overview + pins_arduino.h PIN_NEOPIXEL" }
  },
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },
  "dac": {},
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
